{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set","id":1232172,"title":"Discussing issues with the Solar Craft charm set","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-03T10:46:57-07:00","id":1232172,"title":"Discussing issues with the Solar Craft charm set","content":"I'm involved in a project to create charms for a different set of Exalted, and since that will involve charms that interact with Craft, I wanted to discuss the currently-largest Craft charm set, Solars, and determine what the issues are with it, so as to avoid such pitfalls in our own work.<br /> <br /> Note, this thread is <i>not </i>about discussing the basic Craft system, of project slots, craft XP, and so on. It may not be perfect, but it's what we've got, and I'm actually pretty satisfied with how it works on its own, before charms are applied. So, please, if you want to discuss the pros and cons of the basic Craft system, <i>do it somewhere else</i>. There's plenty of threads.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, I personally think there's two main issues with the Solar Craft charms. First, there's just too flippin' <i>many</i> of them. It's the largest single charm tree currently, weighing in at 56 charms. I like Craft being a hefty charm set, with a lot of things to do, since &quot;peerless craftsmen&quot; is one of the major Solar archetypes. But the charmset currently uses a lot of those charms for what, in my opinion, are rather boring effects - just providing extra slots or craft XP. This also ties into my second big objection to the Craft charms as they stand, that they actually mostly subvert the whole point of the Craft system in general, that it provides a big incentive for a crafting-focused character to use their craft in play, looking for reasons to do crafting to earn craft XP. A whole bunch of Solar Craft charms simply provide a bunch of free craft XP, removing this incentive, and returning the Solar craftsman to their &quot;downtime specialist&quot; focus that they occupied in previous editions.<br /> <br /> So, here's how I'd address both of these issues: cut out a bunch of charms that just provide craft XP, or that make it more efficient. I'd probably cut or heavily modify Ages Echoing Wisdom, Peerless Paragon of Craft, Supreme Perfection of Craft, and Divine Transcendence of Craft - basically, all the charms that just provide free craft XP. I'd merge Tireless Workhorse Method, Dragon Soul Emergence, and God-Forge Within (the slot-granting charms) into a single charm that improves with Essence and repurchases. I'd similarly merge Efficient Craftsman Technique, Copper Spider Conception, and Spirit-Gathering Industry (the charms that deal with making various projects cost less craft XP). I might merge Brass Scales Falling, Red Anvils Ringing, and Chains Fall Away, but I do like how they encourage the actual craft objectives, so maybe not.<br /> <br /> I think these changes would at least condense the charm tree a fair bit, and remove some of the places where it avoids the craft system, rather than building on it. What do people think? Does anyone have any other suggestions about the Solar Craft charms? I'd welcome discussion of other homebrew charms, just as long as, as I said above, we don't get into discussions of the basic crafting system in general, and confine it to Solar or other Exalted charms that take the basic crafting system as their foundation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":1533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","user":"Kelly Pedersen","date":". 07-03-2018, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T13:59:51-07:00","id":1232220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set#post1232172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that out of the way, I personally think there's two main issues with the Solar Craft charms. First, there's just too flippin' <i>many</i> of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, absolutely. My Night Caste has more Craft charms than for Athletics+Awareness+Dodge+Larceny+Stealth put together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd merge Tireless Workhorse Method, Dragon Soul Emergence, and God-Forge Within (the slot-granting charms) into a single charm that improves with Essence and repurchases. </div> </div> </div>So, slots...<br /> The thing about slots is that I've never actually seen them come up. Generally people craft one thing. Sometimes they craft two or three things at the same time, and the ST generally decides if it's reasonable or not (and generally what happens is they work on one thing while another is setting/drying/tanning or whatever).<br /> The only time I've needed to use 2 slots at once is when I made a level 2 artefact.<br /> The only time I've needed to use 3 slots at once is when I made a level 3 artefact.<br /> After I started writing this, I thought &quot;oh no, I can't actually make level 4 artefacts, I don't have 4 slots!&quot; But then I went back and found you can just make another slot for 5 silver points, so... it doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Tireless Workhorse gives you a ton of slots. If you wanted to merge those charms into one, sure, but honestly Tireless Workhorse Method is enough.<br /> <br /> So, for this Exalted set you're writing, yeah, definitely one charm for slots is fine.<br /> (I notice Dragonblood have a grand total of 0 charms relating to slots, unless I've missed one)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This also ties into my second big objection to the Craft charms as they stand, that they actually mostly subvert the whole point of the Craft system in general, that it provides a big incentive for a crafting-focused character to use their craft in play, looking for reasons to do crafting to earn craft XP. A whole bunch of Solar Craft charms simply provide a bunch of free craft XP, removing this incentive, and returning the Solar craftsman to their &quot;downtime specialist&quot; focus that they occupied in previous editions.<br /> So, here's how I'd address both of these issues: cut out a bunch of charms that just provide craft XP, or that make it more efficient. </div> </div> </div>Okay, so this is quite an important one...<br /> I've heard people on this forum say &quot;don't buy Craft XP charms, they're a trap!&quot;<br /> I've heard people say &quot;Craft XP charms ruin the Craft system because they mean you can just ignore the incentive system.&quot; (Not just on the forum, people I play with too)<br /> <br /> But... when I started running 3rd ed, there was an Essence 4 crafter Twilight with 6 craft abilities at 5 (we were continuing our 3rd ed game).<br /> He was a really cool crafter: he made giant walls around a city before a seige, he built a castle of obsidian, he built towns on stilts for merchants outside the jungle where the PCs lived, and giant chains to go across the river so their people could control trade. He built a whole capital for the kingdom.<br /> And he was perpetually short of Craft XP until I got him to buy the Craft XP charms (which took a while, because it's a long tree).<br /> I was often quite generous with his Craft rewards because I felt it was too difficult for him to get Craft XP, but it was still difficult for him.<br /> <br /> Of course, actually he was still short of Craft XP as he bought up Brass Scales Falling, Red Anvils Ringing, Chains Fall Away and Peerless Paragon of Craft.<br /> Then he got Sublime Transference and Supreme Perfection of Craft and within a story he had so much Craft XP that I stopped making him count it (he had something like 300 gold xp).<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I currently play two games. In one, my friend has a Haslanti engineer and skyship captain (named, of course, Cid Highwind). He's got Brass Scales Falling, Red Anvils Ringing, Chains Fall Away and Peerless Paragon of Craft. After about one story, his airship was eaten by a worm, leaving just the artefact engine.<br /> So he needed to make a new non-artefact superior project to make a new hull and balloon. He didn't even have enough gold xp to do that, I convinced the ST to let another Solar crafter make some of the rolls by working on it as well.<br /> <br /> In the other game, I have a crafter with all the same charms as him, plus Sublime Transference and Supreme Perfection of Craft. In 5 sessions I've already made a level 2 artefact, a level 3 artefact and bought about 10 dots of Craft abilities with gold xp.<br /> I've still got 49 gold xp and make 13 more every day; my limitations are materials and time, gold xp is essentially irrelevant to me at this point, unless I went and tried to make an artefact every game or something.<br /> <br /> Essentially, what I'm saying is that Brass Scales Falling, Chains Fall Away and Peerless Paragon of Craft are all rubbish, and Sublime Transference and Supreme Perfection of Craft are extremely overpowered.<br /> <br /> Red Anvils Ringing is probably the only one that's sensibly balanced.<br /> <br /> (Sublime Transference is a bit complicated... it's not really busted by itself, but it's busted in combination with Supreme Perfection or with players who abuse it by doing 100 basic projects in a day. On the other hand, it can be quite important at helping players not get caught out by the system when, say, they've used all their silver xp and everyone's asking them to do a major project, and they have to somehow explain in-character that they physically can't do the major project they've done 20 times before today for some reason.)<br /> <br /> <br /> So, my overall point is... do have a few Craft XP charms, because not all games give crafters the opportunity/motive to do an absolute ton of basic projects (except if the player is jammy and gets sxp from 100 basic projects in a day, which I've seen... but that's probably not how it's supposed to work, and generally something the ST allowed because he was fed up of how the Crafters didn't seem to be able to do something). Just don't make them too good or too bad.<br /> <br /> If you want a more interesting way of generating Craft XP, I've considered maybe more objectives? But you have to be careful; the point of the objectives is to ensure that you only get Craft XP if you do something significant; ie you're supposed to be crafting for a reason, not just to get craft xp (whether that actually works in practice as well is another matter...). So you've got to think carefully about what other objectives will mean it's for stuff that actually matters. Saying, for example, Lunars get craft xp for making stuff out of creatures they've killed sounds obvious, but would mean they'd just make stuff for no purpose beyond silver xp, which isn't really the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does anyone have any other suggestions about the Solar Craft charms? I'd welcome discussion of other homebrew charms, just as long as, as I said above, we don't get into discussions of the basic crafting system in general, and confine it to Solar or other Exalted charms that take the basic crafting system as their foundation. </div> </div> </div>I think my main suggestion would be to have plenty of charms that let you do particular things with craft, rather than just more dice/craft xp/slots.<br /> <br /> For example, the DB craft set includes:<br /> Use Craft for a feat of demolition<br /> Craft an object which does an inspire roll on all who see it<br /> Do a major project as a combat action, for example make a weapon in the middle of a fight<br /> And the normal craft faster and ignore tools, like the Solar set.<br /> <br /> That's not actually that much, but then the DB craft set is pretty small (17 charms including the excellency). I think a little over half the charms are not about dice/slots/terminus/craft XP, whereas for Solars it's about a fifth I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-03-2018, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T15:17:12-07:00","id":1232237,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna point out a particular problem I've noticed in the overall solar charmset but please correct me if I'm wrong. Almost all of the charms that grant free (non-craft) XP are in the craft tree.<br /> <br /> Exegesis of Distilled Form allows a conversion of White XP to regular XP<br /> Spirit-Stoking Elevation allows you to buy several charms directly by using White XP<br /> Supreme Celestial Focus lets you buy dots of craft with gold XP<br /> Design Beyond limit allows you to get an evocation for free.<br /> <br /> The only other charm I know of to gain xp via charm use is in lore. Tireless Learner Method allows you to gain back more xp than you lent out using Flowing Mind Prana. However, this is limited by the fact that it costs xp to use and on average you won't even gain back as much as you spend on it. If you spent 10xp on FMP then on average your first roll would get you 5 xp back. Second roll would only get you 3xp on average. You'd get 8xp back and spend 1 xp that can't be recovered. It's seriously diminishing returns after that. <br /> <br /> Considering that it's possible to get so much craft xp that you eventually just stop keeping track of it (according to some player experience) this would indicate that a craft heavy player could potentially start massively outspending their peers in regular xp. Even if this doesn't count towards essence this raises an eyebrow for me at least. I should note here that given the way the craft ability is structured, I don't think it's a problem to have a charm such as Supreme Celestial Focus to buy up lots of craft. There's a lot of diminishing returns with picking up extra types of craft after all. Not so with general conversion of wxp into xp. <br /> <br /> There are two explanations as to why these charms are in craft: First, there are so many craft charms and abilities that it was ruled unfair to a craft focused players vs other concepts and as such steps were taken to increase a crafter's ability to purchase all the craft charms. Second I think that somewhere along the way the writers stumbled over the terminology of craft <b><i>xp</i></b> and linked it too strongly to actual XP and thus wrote in charms to make them exchangeable. <br /> <br /> I feel that any new craft charm set should do away with any ability to buy XP with craft XP. And also significantly drop the number of craft charms as the OP has suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T17:39:57-07:00","id":1232259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232220#post1232220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about slots is that I've never actually seen them come up. Generally people craft one thing. Sometimes they craft two or three things at the same time, and the ST generally decides if it's reasonable or not (and generally what happens is they work on one thing while another is setting/drying/tanning or whatever).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. That suggests to me that there needs to be more incentives to use the slots you've got. Over in the other <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229940-crafting-system?p=1232244#post1232244\">currently-ongoing craft thread</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> had some interesting suggestions for charm mechanics related to slots. They were in context of Alchemical charms, of course, but I think they could be adapted to Solar Craft just as well. One thing I definitely like the idea of is some effects that give you bonuses for having lots of ongoing projects, and others that let you commit more slots to a single project. I think either effect illustrates the idea that slots are best described as your &quot;focus&quot; in craft. <br /> <br /> The idea of filling multiple slots also suggests a way at least one of the &quot;free craft XP&quot; charms could be rebuilt - make it so that you get craft XP based on the number of currently-occupied project slots you have at the end of a scene/session/story. That would encourage players to keep multiple projects going at once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, what I'm saying is that Brass Scales Falling, Chains Fall Away and Peerless Paragon of Craft are all rubbish, and Sublime Transference and Supreme Perfection of Craft are extremely overpowered.<br /> <br /> Red Anvils Ringing is probably the only one that's sensibly balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think I pretty much agree there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Sublime Transference is a bit complicated... it's not really busted by itself, but it's busted in combination with Supreme Perfection or with players who abuse it by doing 100 basic projects in a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can the &quot;100 basic projects a day&quot; thing be mitigated by compressing them, whenever possible, into a major project? I know that's pretty much canonical for, say, making 100 arrows or knives or something, but even if they're making a teddybear, and then a bauble, and then a knife, and then mending a pot, etc., etc., can you just say &quot;if you're spending the whole day crafting, you just need a major slot, and you get one reward&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, it can be quite important at helping players not get caught out by the system when, say, they've used all their silver xp and everyone's asking them to do a major project, and they have to somehow explain in-character that they physically can't do the major project they've done 20 times before today for some reason.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This I can see as an issue. Although, how difficult is it to find a quickie basic project you can do? Or two, or three, if you can only satisfy one objective with each? It seems to me that if you've got enough time for finishing a major project to be helpful, you've probably always got time to throw in a few basic projects first to build up the silver XP to get started. That goes whether or not you've got Craftsman Needs No Tools, since it speeds up both basic and major projects, so you'd <i>still</i> have time, I'd think.<br /> <br /> That said, there might be room for a charm to get &quot;emergency craft XP&quot; - perhaps something that lets you craft a basic project that relates in some way to the project you actually want to make, and if you meet any objective, you automatically start the major project, ignoring the normal silver XP requirement. This could be extended too - it's probably not balanced to allow a &quot;starter&quot; basic project to work for a superior or legendary project, but I could see it &quot;chaining&quot;, with the basic project allowing you to start a major, and successful completion of the major letting you start a superior, and finally superior lets you start on legendary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a more interesting way of generating Craft XP, I've considered maybe more objectives? But you have to be careful; the point of the objectives is to ensure that you only get Craft XP if you do something significant; ie you're supposed to be crafting for a reason, not just to get craft xp (whether that actually works in practice as well is another matter...). So you've got to think carefully about what other objectives will mean it's for stuff that actually matters. Saying, for example, Lunars get craft xp for making stuff out of creatures they've killed sounds obvious, but would mean they'd just make stuff for no purpose beyond silver xp, which isn't really the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd want to be very careful about adding more objectives. On the other hand, improving the rewards from the existing objectives seems like more fertile ground. The one about your own intimacies, for example, could give more craft XP based on the strength of the intimacy, and so could the one based on other people's intimacies toward you. I'm less sure about the &quot;material benefit&quot; one - that tends to be its own reward, so giving more craft XP based on the value of the reward seems a bit off. But there's probably something there. And an effect to give you more if you meet multiple goals sounds like it has potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T18:02:12-07:00","id":1232265,"title":"","content":"As a general thought on the Solar Charmset:<br /> <br /> You can do a huge amount of reduction (part of the problem really) by condensing some of the Charms into a single Charm that automatically upgrades as Craft X/Essence X. We don't need three Charms that add slots, they're not that potent, as already mentioned. So a Charm that gives you more Major at C1/E1, more Superior at C3/E3, and more Legendary at C5/E5. Two less Charms (including one that requires repurchases per slot), no function lost, less clutter of this sort of Charm in the trees.<br /> <br /> The Craft Charms seem really obsessed with forcing repeat Charms for Basic/Major projects, then Superior/Legendary ones (if not split those two up to), which adds to the bloat with little positive impact. If gating off bonuses to higher ranked projects is important, you can do automatic upgrade Charms. Buying new Charms should really do something new, instead of, &quot;remove the restriction of using the Charm on this thing,&quot; in something as big as the Craft Charms.<br /> <br /> On my whole weird Charm Slots as Charm currency thing? I actually initially envisioned it for Solars. I just though that it could work better for Alchemicals when someone brought up Alchemicals in that thread, because it has a neat feel towards their Charm style (assuming it doesn't change in 3e).<br /> <br /> When I was first thinking about it, I was still sticking to the figurative idea of it. A Solar isn't literally a walking workshop, but their excellence lets them make things with little to nothing like even the best mortal craftspeople need workshops for. It just seemed that the Charm aesthetic for the Alchemicals let them be actual workshops if you slot in the right Craft Charms and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T18:50:27-07:00","id":1232270,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8804_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8804\" data-vbnamecard=\"8804\">armyofwhispers</a><br /> <br /> You are super overestimating Exegesis of the Distilled Form, have Spirit-Stoking Elevation completely wrong, and are slightly underestimating Tireless Learner Method.<br /> <br /> -Exegesis of the Distilled Form:<br /> <br /> This is a very hard Charm to actually get to use. You need to complete 5 Legendary Projects before you get to use it. That is the creation of <b><i><u>5</u></i></b> N/A Level Artifacts/Manses, wonders of Creation shaking power.<br /> <br /> You have to amass empire ruining amounts of resources, extremely rare components, and have reached the height of Solar crafting power to be able to complete the works.<br /> <br /> I`d say the Charm Suite that will let you amass enough Craft XP, Craft Power, and speed to do this is around 25 Charms. That is 200 Experience. The limit EotDF gives you per activation is 20 Exp. So to even break even on your Craft investment will take you making 50 equivalents of Eyes of Autotochton, Mantles of Brigid, Emerald Thuribles, Ascendant Nova Phoenixes or Karvaras. And at the very minimum 10 stories, which could range from anywhere from 20 to 80 sessions, which with weekly play would take from 5 months to an year and a half.<br /> <br /> That is if you manage to make 5 of the most powerful objects the world has ever seen <b><i><u>every godamn story.</u></i></b><br /> <br /> So no, EotDF is not a concern out of crazy white rooming. Consider yourself lucky if you get to use it a few times in the whole campaign, and in a long running campaign at that. That is if you're a Craft Supernal that invest super heavily in it. Most people will never get to use it.<br /> <br /> -Spirit-Stoking Elevation:<br /> <br /> This will let you fuel Lore, Occult and Medicine Charms that cost Experience with White Craft Experience by paying 5 WExp for every Experience. It does not let you buy Charms.<br /> <br /> -Tireless Learner Method:<br /> <br /> You actually roll all your Experience until you recover it. This was clarified by Vance a while ago.<br /> <br /> So lets say in Story 1 you invest 10 Experience in Flowing Mind Prana. At the end of Story 1 you roll (and re-roll non successes once) and you get 5 sucesses, one of which is a 10, So you recover 6 Experience and keep 5 Experience to reroll at the end of the nest Story.<br /> <br /> So you basically will never come up short, and every 10 you manage to roll is a bonus Experience you get.<br /> <br /> -Wrap up:<br /> <br /> So, there are some Experience shenenigans, but they involve Spirit-Stoking Elevation and Lore Teaching Charms, but this will let you give insane amount of Experience to other people, and even then at mid to high Essence levels, unless your Circle builds around and for it (and rotates who is teaching), and even then it will be limited by story constraints such as training times, and allowing the teacher to basically brainwash your character.<br /> <br /> It is not a great problem, it is one very specific, mid-high Essence build, that very few people will stumble upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 07-03-2018, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T20:55:26-07:00","id":1232297,"title":"","content":"Solar Craft's main sins, to me, are a fewfold.<br /> <br /> 1) It over-values some resources. As noted already, it kind of puts too much work into slots. I think that in the end, there needed to be like...a slots Charm, tops. Something I did with my own houserules is at least have it so that if you're swimming in slots you could just <i>do more</i> with them. But in the base system, there's no need for a Charm to discount them, one to give you permaentns and then a later one to give you permanents fo antoher kind. Slots aren't <i>that</i> expensive, and that the Charms themselves can be overly complciated (Copper Spider Concentration is a mess) don't help.<br /> <br /> 2) It undervalues other things too. The extra craft xp Charms are not bad until you get to Peerless Paragon of Craft, which then more or less explodes the entire damned craft xp economy, invalidates every previous Charm, and to boot, kind of helps you circumvent ever doing things with rolls really to get craft xp again. This is before that again, they're spread out probably over too many Charms and often have systems that are more complext han they need to be, or in the case of I think the first couple, give so little real xp that they tend to rot on your character sheet after a bit.<br /> <br /> 3) A few of the Repair Charms have special highlight for being just really bad. This is in part because it seems like Morke might not have been clear that repairing is prettye asy, and anything that buffs normal craft will buff repairing things. As such, the Charms are pretty niche since they basically are like the already over-common broader Charms but to a specific task, and often are flat-out worse than the more general Charm. <br /> <br /> 4) The Power tree is actually not bad like, in powerwise. It lets Solars achieve pretty impressive feats of artifice. The issue is that I think while I like dice tricks, they kind of are insane about them. Things like triple-10s, buncha weird rerolls, the different double-Ns upgrade Charm. And even a Charm that lets you get more Charms, which I gather is just asking for player decision paralysis. The houserule set I use is by someone who did what they could to get the same general results, but with like...half the Charms and complexity. I think that it's not a question these Charms are bad, it's a question on whether these are Charms people would actually find enjoyable and I think they are where the threshold of fidgety dice tricks gets overkill for many.<br /> <br /> 5) There's a general trend I think with above of over-complication in general actually. Like, Focus-Shifitng Arete isn't a terrible Charm, but in the end, it's a lot of dice rolling and such to get over a +1 difficulty. Like....it should just be spend points, get effect. I think there are a few Charms in the Solar Charmset like this in general, mind. But this one always stands out to me as it's so much work for the effect it gives. <br /> <br /> 6) There's a notable lack I think of cool &quot;wiz-bang&quot; effects. Craftsman Needs No Tools, Vice-Miracle Technique, Dual-Magnus Prana, and the such are <i>cool</i> powers. But there's not really so much there like those. The houserules I use currently I like most in part because it has a few like that, like one that makes your workshop <i>yours</i> in a style similar to Ship-Claiming Stance for instance, or one that has this effect like a Dr. Who Sonic Screwdirver Artifact. I think a bit of the interest in making clever system tricks rather than Charms that made Craft characterful was a bit of a shame. More stuff to play on Crafting with Intimacies, Crafting towards specific kinds of things like food or art, branding, workshops, all that. I think the Solar Craft Charms focus oddly too much on Craft the system more than it needed to and didn't put as much into Crafting characters as it should.<br /> <br /> It's kind of similar to some other trees that I have felt a bit sour towards in Solar Craft, like how Solar Survival focuses way more on being a beast master than a survivalist than I'd of liked.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, those are to me the big ones. This is again, someone who actaully likes the base Craft system overall. But I do think that if there's a of the Exalted system I'm often let down on in further look, it's Craft Charms and I think they highlight in kind of an extreme way many things folks have issues with in small parts around the rest of the system in a big way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T22:13:09-07:00","id":1232312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232270#post1232270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8804_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8804\" data-vbnamecard=\"8804\">armyofwhispers</a><br /> <br /> You are super overestimating Exegesis of the Distilled Form, have Spirit-Stoking Elevation completely wrong, and are slightly underestimating Tireless Learner Method.<br /> <br /> -Exegesis of the Distilled Form:<br /> <br /> This is a very hard Charm to actually get to use. You need to complete 5 Legendary Projects before you get to use it. That is the creation of <b><i><u>5</u></i></b> N/A Level Artifacts/Manses, wonders of Creation shaking power.<br /> <br /> You have to amass empire ruining amounts of resources, extremely rare components, and have reached the height of Solar crafting power to be able to complete the works.<br /> <br /> I`d say the Charm Suite that will let you amass enough Craft XP, Craft Power, and speed to do this is around 25 Charms. That is 200 Experience. The limit EotDF gives you per activation is 20 Exp. So to even break even on your Craft investment will take you making 50 equivalents of Eyes of Autotochton, Mantles of Brigid, Emerald Thuribles, Ascendant Nova Phoenixes or Karvaras. And at the very minimum 10 stories, which could range from anywhere from 20 to 80 sessions, which with weekly play would take from 5 months to an year and a half.<br /> <br /> That is if you manage to make 5 of the most powerful objects the world has ever seen <b><i><u>every godamn story.</u></i></b><br /> <br /> So no, EotDF is not a concern out of crazy white rooming. Consider yourself lucky if you get to use it a few times in the whole campaign, and in a long running campaign at that. That is if you're a Craft Supernal that invest super heavily in it. Most people will never get to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is unlikely to come up, granted. and it take a whole hell of a lot to get there BUT there is currently no charm that gives you xp of any kind for killing 5 nigh-unkillable things or stealing 5 unstealable things or... etc.<br /> <br /> While it takes a whole hell of a lot of setup, it remains the case that it's still absent from the rest of the charmset.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232270#post1232270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Spirit-Stoking Elevation:<br /> <br /> This will let you fuel Lore, Occult and Medicine Charms that cost Experience with White Craft Experience by paying 5 WExp for every Experience. It does not let you buy Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, you're quite right! That's much <i>much</i> worse since a single attempt at wyld shaping could cost you dozens of xp normally. Still, it's at least potentially transient xp and it's not like you'd get that back if you fail the rolls so I withdraw my objection about it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232270#post1232270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Tireless Learner Method:<br /> <br /> You actually roll all your Experience until you recover it. This was clarified by Vance a while ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid you may have misunderstood. You can reroll xp lent out using Flowing Mind Prana until you have it all back. However, each time you activate Tireless Learner Method it costs 1 xp to use. This xp is <i>not</i> rerolled and is only recovered if you get lucky when you roll for the xp from FMP<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232270#post1232270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So lets say in Story 1 you invest 10 Experience in Flowing Mind Prana. At the end of Story 1 you roll (and re-roll non successes once) and you get 5 sucesses, one of which is a 10, So you recover 6 Experience and keep 5 Experience to reroll at the end of the nest Story.<br /> <br /> So you basically will never come up short, and every 10 you manage to roll is a bonus Experience you get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm... what are you talking about? 10s don't matter at all for either Flowing Mind Prana or Tireless Learner Method except as regular double successes. You don't get any extra from tens.<br /> <br /> Let's compare math:<br /> <br /> You invest 10xp in flowing mind prana. Each die has a 1 in 10 chance of every result and 4 of those results are successes (tens count double of course) so on average you'll roll approximately 4 successful results one of which is a ten (on average). Therefore your average of a roll of 10 dice is 5 successes. Full stop.<br /> <br /> Next, You spend 1 xp on TLM and get to reroll failed dice from before. That leaves (on average) 6 dice to roll. Once again you average out to 3 successes. You don't get to reroll fails any more.<br /> <br /> Your total is 8 successes. So you get 8 xp back.<br /> <br /> At the end of the next story you have the option of spending another 1 xp to use TLM again but YOU ONLY GET TO ROLL 2 DICE. This is the problem. Your average on that roll is slightly more than 1 success and oh look, that makes up the 10 xp you originally spent on FMP and you're still down the 2 xp from your two uses of TLM. And now you have no more dice to roll to regain xp until your next use of FMP.<br /> <br /> This is what I mean that it's an xp sink. The only way to <i>gain </i>xp from TLM is if you have a good number of dice to roll from FMP and you manage to get more successes than missing dice AND the cost of the charm to allow the cap break. Otherwise the cap of FMP stands at the same amount you initially gave away and you're out any xp spent on TLM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232270#post1232270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Wrap up:<br /> <br /> So, there are some Experience shenenigans, but they involve Spirit-Stoking Elevation and Lore Teaching Charms, but this will let you give insane amount of Experience to other people, and even then at mid to high Essence levels, unless your Circle builds around and for it (and rotates who is teaching), and even then it will be limited by story constraints such as training times, and allowing the teacher to basically brainwash your character.<br /> <br /> It is not a great problem, it is one very specific, mid-high Essence build, that very few people will stumble upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with it isn't so much that it's gonna be a common thing (far from it) my issue is more that it's the only place in the entire charmset that allows you to bypass xp costs.Every single one of them is in craft (unless you get really lucky with TLM).<br /> <br /> One thing I will note is that you can use Flowing Mind Prana and Spirit-Stoking Elevation to use your insane amount of craft xp to boost up your entire party with real xp. I'm not sure that the writers knew how much white xp was available to a dedicated crafter. And here again, it's ONLY the craft end that's really feasible. It takes a three charm dip and lore 5 to get the training charm, while the craft end is... daunting. So I guess... craft is the skill to really boost everybody's xp? But only in certain limited ways? I dunno, it just seems really weird to dump all that into craft and why is xp bypassing charms even in the solar charmset at all? It seems like really questionable design space to be able to train past xp limits. At least training PCs that is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should really distill my post here. My objection is not &quot;These things are super problematic we should fix them&quot; Its: &quot;Why are these effects here <i>at all</i>. If they have to be here, why are <i>all </i>of them in <i>craft?&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 07-04-2018, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T22:36:28-07:00","id":1232315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232270#post1232270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8804_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8804\" data-vbnamecard=\"8804\">armyofwhispers</a><br /> <br /> You are super overestimating Exegesis of the Distilled Form, have Spirit-Stoking Elevation completely wrong, and are slightly underestimating Tireless Learner Method.<br /> <br /> -Exegesis of the Distilled Form:<br /> <br /> This is a very hard Charm to actually get to use. You need to complete 5 Legendary Projects before you get to use it. That is the creation of <b><i><u>5</u></i></b> N/A Level Artifacts/Manses, wonders of Creation shaking power.<br /> <br /> You have to amass empire ruining amounts of resources, extremely rare components, and have reached the height of Solar crafting power to be able to complete the works.<br /> <br /> I`d say the Charm Suite that will let you amass enough Craft XP, Craft Power, and speed to do this is around 25 Charms. That is 200 Experience. The limit EotDF gives you per activation is 20 Exp. So to even break even on your Craft investment will take you making 50 equivalents of Eyes of Autotochton, Mantles of Brigid, Emerald Thuribles, Ascendant Nova Phoenixes or Karvaras. And at the very minimum 10 stories, which could range from anywhere from 20 to 80 sessions, which with weekly play would take from 5 months to an year and a half.<br /> <br /> That is if you manage to make 5 of the most powerful objects the world has ever seen <b><i><u>every godamn story.</u></i></b><br /> <br /> So no, EotDF is not a concern out of crazy white rooming. Consider yourself lucky if you get to use it a few times in the whole campaign, and in a long running campaign at that. That is if you're a Craft Supernal that invest super heavily in it. Most people will never get to use it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>OMG the Twilight crafter in my game was totally abusing the hell out of that and don't think he ever completed 5 NA projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T00:42:22-07:00","id":1232328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232312#post1232312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid you may have misunderstood. You can reroll xp lent out using Flowing Mind Prana until you have it all back. However, each time you activate Tireless Learner Method it costs 1 xp to use. This xp is <i>not</i> rerolled and is only recovered if you get lucky when you roll for the xp from FMP</div> </div> </div> </div>I teach someone 10xp of stuff with Flowing Mind Prana. The story ends. I roll 10 dice and get 6 successes. I have 4xp committed left. Without TLM, I cannot recover more than 10xp, period.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 3e Core, Flowing Mind Prana</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of each story, the Solar may roll a number of dice equal to experience points spent on this Charm, regaining a number of experience equal to her successes, but not beyond the total amount of experience she expended in training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tireless Learner Method lets me go &quot;holy shit that was a lucky roll&quot; and spend 1xp to reroll all non-successes, both expediting the recovery and potentially exceeding what I gain. So let's say I roll those 4 dice end of next story, and get three 10s. Normally this would be an overage of 2xp unused. TLM lets me spend 1xp to reroll the one die showing a 1-6 in hopes of getting a 7-10, and keep the 2-4xp overage, ending up 1-3xp ahead of where I was when I loaned it out.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 3e Core, Tireless Learner Method</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of each story, the Solar may roll a number of dice equal to experience points spent on this Charm, regaining a number of experience equal to her successes, but not beyond the total amount of experience she expended in training.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T00:50:17-07:00","id":1232329,"title":"","content":"The Lore teaching Charms I think suffer greatly from a similar problem to my notes on Arete-Shifting Prana. Namely that they're overly &quot;fiddly&quot; mechanics that could have been much easier doen in a simpler manner. I think experience debt, like what was re-introduced in WFHW's manuscript, is generally a better system than manipulating XP and all the general dumbness/randomness that results from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T00:52:53-07:00","id":1232330,"title":"","content":"Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1533_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1533\" data-vbnamecard=\"1533\">Kelly Pedersen</a>, it's kind of shilly, but some of the ideas you have (like merging the slot-making Charms) are in a version of Charms I use based on Nihnoz's work. He did some good ideas and did some things like I noted with making the Power Charms less well, fiddly but with more or less simlar math to tweak to taste. If you want the link is there:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/7r0q37m87o7zr9f/Solar%20Craft%20Charms%20Revised%20v5.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/7r0q37m87o7zr9f/Solar%20Craft%20Charms%20Revised%20v5.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/7r0q37m87o7zr9f/Solar%20Craft%20Charms%20Revised%20v5.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.dropbox.com/s/7r0q37m87o7zr9f/Solar%20Craft%20Charms%20Revised%20v5.pdf?dl=0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T03:10:36-07:00","id":1232340,"title":"","content":"I mean maybe this is from the fact that training times are often stupidly long and are also part of the problem with scaling XP that is my great bugbear, but I think that the Solar training charms are in fact intended as written to 1) allow the beneficiary to *permanently* advance beyond their own EXP totals [rather than just bypass training times], and 2) with TLM, potentially allow the teacher to derive an XP benefit as well, rather than what would happen with XP debt, which would eliminate one of the two; either the beneficiary just gets their XP &quot;prespent, early&quot;, or the teacher doesn't ever recover anything beyond what they invested.<br /> <br /> Whether this is a good or bad design is up to the person in question but I think &quot;gain things beyond what your XP would allow, for a temporary sacrifice on my part that may reap rewards beyond what I invest&quot; is a little more interesting than &quot;get a few dots' worth of XP ahead of time, but once it's paid off you're back at balanced, and I go back to null&quot;. I think a different mechanic for interacting with teaching NPCs would be a good idea, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T05:06:51-07:00","id":1232345,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8804_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8804\" data-vbnamecard=\"8804\">armyofwhispers</a> <br /> <br /> -EotDF<br /> <br /> Craft doesn't let you parry what cannot be parried, dodge what cannot be dodged or take a mountain to the head with no consequence. Different is different.<br /> <br /> To kill and steal things is very different from making things, both narrative and system wise. <br /> <br /> The &quot;Kill Shit&quot; Charm Investment is at most what? 5-6 for a Capstone? Steal stuff is what? 4-5?<br /> <br /> By choosing to delve into Craft you are investing in a portion of the game that will get less showtime than most others.<br /> <br /> These effects are in Craft because it is a massive tree and the Devs thought that giving you an extremely hard way to recoup some of the absolutely massive investment that you made was warranted. And I think that is fine.<br /> <br /> Unless the game has an unusual focus on building stuff, I see no reason to bother with this.<br /> <br /> It is extremely gated.<br /> <br /> -TLM<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"756\" data-vbnamecard=\"756\">Meianno Yuurei</a> clarified this already. The committed Experience only fades when it is recouped, and Tireless Learner Method gives the role re-roll failures once and double 10s, this was settled by Vance on Ask the Devs a while ago.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T05:09:13-07:00","id":1232346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gfrobbin84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232315#post1232315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OMG the Twilight crafter in my game was totally abusing the hell out of that and don't think he ever completed 5 NA projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, people overlook the massive fee to ride on this.<br /> <br /> Hope you have time to correct the course, because if not for that gate it is incredibly broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:46:43-07:00","id":1232371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232237#post1232237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna point out a particular problem I've noticed in the overall solar charmset but please correct me if I'm wrong. Almost all of the charms that grant free (non-craft) XP are in the craft tree.<br /> <br /> Considering that it's possible to get so much craft xp that you eventually just stop keeping track of it (according to some player experience) this would indicate that a craft heavy player could potentially start massively outspending their peers in regular xp. Even if this doesn't count towards essence this raises an eyebrow for me at least</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily, the charm for getting tons of craft xp is at the top of one tree, and the charm for turning White XP into actual XP is at the top of a different tree. A tree chock-full of rubbish (I'd argue it's one of the worst trees Solars can buy; there's a few good bits, like the one where you make a free level 2 artefact once a story, or the pinnacle charm where you clone yourself, but a lot of it is speedbumps). And you have to have completed like 5 legendary projects before that or something, and it's once a story... honestly, it seems like it's totally broken, but I suspect no-one's going to be doing it* unless they've got something like 600xp already, or their character is rubbish, because they sunk all their xp into getting an xp-generating combo that doesn't go anywhere.<br /> <br /> *I've just read the post above this, and it sounds like someone has done it, but by cheating. I've only ever seen one legendary project in-game, I've never seen anyone do more than that.<br /> <br /> Still...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel that any new craft charm set should do away with any ability to buy XP with craft XP. And also significantly drop the number of craft charms as the OP has suggested. </div> </div> </div>This does seem pretty reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:58:37-07:00","id":1232375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232328#post1232328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I teach someone 10xp of stuff with Flowing Mind Prana. The story ends. I roll 10 dice and get 6 successes. I have 4xp committed left. Without TLM, I cannot recover more than 10xp, period.<br /> <br /> Tireless Learner Method lets me go &quot;holy shit that was a lucky roll&quot; and spend 1xp to reroll all non-successes, both expediting the recovery and potentially exceeding what I gain. So let's say I roll those 4 dice end of next story, and get three 10s. Normally this would be an overage of 2xp unused. TLM lets me spend 1xp to reroll the one die showing a 1-6 in hopes of getting a 7-10, and keep the 2-4xp overage, ending up 1-3xp ahead of where I was when I loaned it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, as I said it's certainly <i>possible </i>to gain back more xp than you've spent but on average you won't. On average it's an xp sink. It's like people planning for retirement by buying loto tickets. A bad investment is still a bad investment. To me the main utility of Tireless Learner Method is simply to gain back xp faster than normal. Using it as an xp booster is a mugs game.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that nothing in Tireless Learner Method says that you can roll it after the fact so by standard charm rules you have to declare you're using it <i>before the roll. </i>Thus in your example, you'd just lose the extra 2xp and have no chance of recovering them. <br /> <br /> However, this isn't the thread for it, so if you'd like I'm willing to create another thread to discuss the interaction of Tireless Leaner Method in detail. Or we could ask the devs to clarify the charm again.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2746_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2746\" data-vbnamecard=\"2746\">TGUEIROS</a> First off, we can play the game of which skills give you what all day, melee doesn't let you craft a daiklaive. Stealth doesn't let you build a manse. OBVIOUSLY. Why then, does craft include in it's wheelhouse not one, but <i>four</i> different charms that allow you to bypass experience costs and the regular character advancement path that everyone else must adhere to?<br /> <br /> TLM:<br /> Feel free to search the ask the Devs thread, but when I did I couldn't find anything about being able to always recoup the cost of TLM or being able to activate it after the fact. Also you seem fixated on the double tens thing but as far as I can tell, the roll always had double tens as any other roll would. I have never, not once, said that you cannot recoup the cost spent on FMP. Not once in all my posts.<br /> But let me be as clear as I can: Flowing Mind Prana is not a bad investment. Everything that goes out will come back eventually. Tireless Learner Method <i>is</i> a bad investment. It costs xp to use and gives very bad odds on making it back and very, <i>very</i> bad odds of actually coming out ahead with it. It's only true benefit is to gain back xp from FMP faster than normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:59:58-07:00","id":1232377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232259#post1232259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. That suggests to me that there needs to be more incentives to use the slots you've got.... One thing I definitely like the idea of is some effects that give you bonuses for having lots of ongoing projects, and others that let you commit more slots to a single project. I think either effect illustrates the idea that slots are best described as your &quot;focus&quot; in craft.<br /> <br /> The idea of filling multiple slots also suggests a way at least one of the &quot;free craft XP&quot; charms could be rebuilt - make it so that you get craft XP based on the number of currently-occupied project slots you have at the end of a scene/session/story. That would encourage players to keep multiple projects going at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably something worth considering, yes.<br /> <br /> I'd be a bit careful with rewarding people for keeping multiple projects open, as it might encourage them not to actually finish them, but it's worth exploring.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can the &quot;100 basic projects a day&quot; thing be mitigated by compressing them, whenever possible, into a major project? I know that's pretty much canonical for, say, making 100 arrows or knives or something, but even if they're making a teddybear, and then a bauble, and then a knife, and then mending a pot, etc., etc., can you just say &quot;if you're spending the whole day crafting, you just need a major slot, and you get one reward&quot;? </div> </div> </div>That's how I've house-ruled it, but the rules don't really seem to talk about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although, how difficult is it to find a quickie basic project you can do? Or two, or three, if you can only satisfy one objective with each? It seems to me that if you've got enough time for finishing a major project to be helpful, you've probably always got time to throw in a few basic projects first to build up the silver XP to get started. That goes whether or not you've got Craftsman Needs No Tools, since it speeds up both basic and major projects, so you'd <i>still</i> have time, I'd think. </div> </div> </div>The very first session I ran of 3rd ed, the Twilight with Craft (Weaponsmith) 5 wanted to forge himself a good-quality sword. That's pretty obviously a major project (it's one of the examples). It would take him 5 minutes with Craftsman Needs No Tools.<br /> Technically, he couldn't do it. Yeah, I could have said &quot;go do 3 basic projects, each one only takes 5 seconds) but I didn't see any value in making him think of several basic projects, roll the dice, etc. Essentially, it's just odd, versimilitude-wise, and slows the game down.<br /> I mean, I don't think that Morke and Holden actually wrote the system with the idea that people would go &quot;hmmm, I need to do a major project, I need to think of several basic projects I can shoe-horn into this scene.&quot; I think the whole point of the objectives was that you're supposed to do stuff that actually matters. (Which makes it even more awkward to shoe-horn into a scene just so you can get enough silver for a major project).<br /> <br /> In the end, I just house-ruled that he started with 20 silver xp to get him going. But I've seen this come up with other crafters too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, there might be room for a charm to get &quot;emergency craft XP&quot; - perhaps something that lets you craft a basic project that relates in some way to the project you actually want to make, and if you meet any objective, you automatically start the major project, ignoring the normal silver XP requirement. This could be extended too - it's probably not balanced to allow a &quot;starter&quot; basic project to work for a superior or legendary project, but I could see it &quot;chaining&quot;, with the basic project allowing you to start a major, and successful completion of the major letting you start a superior, and finally superior lets you start on legendary. </div> </div> </div>That seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, improving the rewards from the existing objectives seems like more fertile ground. The one about your own intimacies, for example, could give more craft XP based on the strength of the intimacy, and so could the one based on other people's intimacies toward you. I'm less sure about the &quot;material benefit&quot; one - that tends to be its own reward, so giving more craft XP based on the value of the reward seems a bit off. But there's probably something there. And an effect to give you more if you meet multiple goals sounds like it has potential. </div> </div> </div>Those sound like good ideas. I don't think the one about meeting multiple objectives is necessary (there's already a big benefit, because you're already getting a fair bit of craft xp), but it's not problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T08:06:01-07:00","id":1232381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232297#post1232297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Craft's main sins, to me, are a fewfold.<br /> <br /> 1) It over-values some resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) It undervalues other things too. The extra craft xp Charms are not bad until you get to Peerless Paragon of Craft, which then more or less explodes the entire damned craft xp economy, invalidates every previous Charm, and to boot, kind of helps you circumvent ever doing things with rolls really to get craft xp again. </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) A few of the Repair Charms have special highlight for being just really bad. </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) The Power tree is actually not bad like, in powerwise. It lets Solars achieve pretty impressive feats of artifice. The issue is that I think while I like dice tricks, they kind of are insane about them. Things like triple-10s, buncha weird rerolls, the different double-Ns upgrade Charm. </div> </div> </div>They're even more complex when combined. I had to write this to explain how to make a craft roll with 2 power charms:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">20 dice<br /> <br /> Flawless Handiwork Method (re-roll 10s)<br /> <br /> Bright-Forging Prana (1/story):<br /> <br /> [Supreme Masterwork Focus x3 (double 7s)<br /> <br /> Experiential Conjuring of the Void (1 success and 10 extra dice, all non-charm)<br /> <br /> Unbroken Image Focus (5 extra successes plus 1 per success rolled before double 9s, all non-charm)]<br /> <br /> So, in conclusion:<br /> Roll 20 dice with re-roll 10s<br /> <br /> 7s, 8s and 9s are each worth 3 successes, 10s are worth 4<br /> <br /> Then roll another 10 dice with re-roll 10s and double 7s<br /> (so they're just worth 2 each this time)<br /> <br /> Now add 6 successes <br /> <br /> Now take away 4 (because the roll is difficulty 5)<br /> <br /> You need 100 total, and can't roll more than 6 times.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even a Charm that lets you get more Charms, which I gather is just asking for player decision paralysis. </div> </div> </div>It's kind of good for people who just want to craft an artefact occasionally without buying a ton of charms. (It's once/story)<br /> I was going to buy it for my crafter, but then I realised that with 2 other charms I can make level 2-3 artefacts easily, and not just once a story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) There's a general trend I think with above of over-complication in general actually. Like, Focus-Shifitng Arete </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) There's a notable lack I think of cool &quot;wiz-bang&quot; effects. Craftsman Needs No Tools, Vice-Miracle Technique, Dual-Magnus Prana, and the such are <i>cool</i> powers. But there's not really so much there like those. </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> I think this probably covers most of the issues.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T08:18:31-07:00","id":1232386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8804_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8804\" data-vbnamecard=\"8804\">armyofwhispers</a> <br /> <br /> Sorry friend, I'm not playing any kinds of games here. You were the one to bring this up and I responded in kind. It is you complaining that one Ability has a thing no other Ability has. When there are plenty Abilities that have many things others don't have,<br /> <br /> My position is simple, there is nothing in EotDF that merits much changing if you use it as written and play an actual game, instead of theorizing about one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T09:49:45-07:00","id":1232412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232297#post1232297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) There's a notable lack I think of cool &quot;wiz-bang&quot; effects. Craftsman Needs No Tools, Vice-Miracle Technique, Dual-Magnus Prana, and the such are <i>cool</i> powers. But there's not really so much there like those. The houserules I use currently I like most in part because it has a few like that, like one that makes your workshop <i>yours</i> in a style similar to Ship-Claiming Stance for instance, or one that has this effect like a Dr. Who Sonic Screwdirver Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea of &quot;claiming&quot; a workshop. What about the &quot;sonic screwdriver&quot; thing - what's the effect there? <br /> <br /> I definitely agree in general that the charmset needs more cool things, rather than just dice tricks and slots and craft xp and so on. One idea I've been playing around with, actually, is a charm that lets you &quot;encode&quot; one of your Intimacies into a thing you craft, and then everyone who looks at it will automatically know which intimacy is there, and people who use the object in a way that upholds that intimacy would get some kind of bonus. I'm not sure how to handle that bonus, though. I'd like it to be bigger than just &quot;exceptional tool&quot; level, but I'd rather not make it artifact-level either. Also, I think the strength of your intimacy should play into the level of the bonus, but how to do that without having your Defining intimacy be the only one you ever use? Maybe the bonus depends on the level of the intimacy encoded, but only people who have that intimacy at some level can get the full bonus?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd definitely like suggestions for more cool Craft charms. Did you ever write up the &quot;Workshop-Claiming Stance&quot; or &quot;sonic screwdriver&quot; charms, and if so, would you be willing to post them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232377#post1232377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be a bit careful with rewarding people for keeping multiple projects open, as it might encourage them not to actually finish them, but it's worth exploring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably say you have to make a roll for at least one interval during the story for it to count as an ongoing project. I guess that would mean it would only apply to Superior and Legendary projects, though, since they're the only ones with intervals. Have to think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very first session I ran of 3rd ed, the Twilight with Craft (Weaponsmith) 5 wanted to forge himself a good-quality sword. That's pretty obviously a major project (it's one of the examples). It would take him 5 minutes with Craftsman Needs No Tools.<br /> Technically, he couldn't do it. Yeah, I could have said &quot;go do 3 basic projects, each one only takes 5 seconds) but I didn't see any value in making him think of several basic projects, roll the dice, etc. Essentially, it's just odd, versimilitude-wise, and slows the game down.<br /> <br /> In the end, I just house-ruled that he started with 20 silver xp to get him going. But I've seen this come up with other crafters too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, yeah - like you, I've houseruled that crafters start with some craft XP to get going. But the minor project &quot;busywork&quot; can still be irritating, I can definitely get that. I wonder if there's room, in either the basic craft system or as a charm, to go into &quot;craft XP debt&quot; - maybe allow you to start a major project without any xp, but the cost comes out of the reward?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:09:26-07:00","id":1232417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232412#post1232412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like the idea of &quot;claiming&quot; a workshop. What about the &quot;sonic screwdriver&quot; thing - what's the effect there?<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the link I have to the houserules I use. It's basically a Charm that creates a specail device that then allows one to do First Age Artifice without sorcery. A friend of mine noted that in his mind, it looked liek a sonic screwdriver which well, it can kind of I damit.<br /> <br /> Words-as-Workshops Method can pull it off too, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:25:06-07:00","id":1232426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232417#post1232417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in the link I have to the houserules I use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your &quot;Craft Houserules&quot; link in your sig is giving me a 404 error when I click on it. Did you post another link that I didn't spot somewhere?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's basically a Charm that creates a specail device that then allows one to do First Age Artifice without sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Interesting thought. Does it also eliminate the other requirements, like infrastructure? I'm not sure I like the idea of letting Solar crafters rebuild the First Age <i>too</i> easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:30:16-07:00","id":1232431,"title":"","content":"The Solar Charmset has ALWAYS suffered for being the first one written for each new addition of the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:31:24-07:00","id":1232432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232431#post1232431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar Charmset has ALWAYS suffered for being the first one written for each new addition of the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an inherent problem. You can't help but wonder how much more playtesting might've occured without the leak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:46:32-07:00","id":1232439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232432#post1232432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an inherent problem. You can't help but wonder how much more playtesting might've occured without the leak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or without the unproductive attitude towards the leak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:47:15-07:00","id":1232440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232417#post1232417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in the link I have to the houserules I use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, nevermind the question about the link to these - I spotted the link you posted upthread, and that one works. Apologies again for the misunderstanding!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T11:17:00-07:00","id":1232446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232375#post1232375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, as I said it's certainly <i>possible </i>to gain back more xp than you've spent but on average you won't. On average it's an xp sink. It's like people planning for retirement by buying loto tickets. A bad investment is still a bad investment. To me the main utility of Tireless Learner Method is simply to gain back xp faster than normal. Using it as an xp booster is a mugs game.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that nothing in Tireless Learner Method says that you can roll it after the fact so by standard charm rules you have to declare you're using it <i>before the roll. </i>Thus in your example, you'd just lose the extra 2xp and have no chance of recovering them.<br /> <br /> However, this isn't the thread for it, so if you'd like I'm willing to create another thread to discuss the interaction of Tireless Leaner Method in detail. Or we could ask the devs to clarify the charm again.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1103132#post1103132\">The Exp you commit to Flowing Mind Prana is Committed until recovered So it is always a net positive amount of exp.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1153512#post1153512\">Also EXP given by flowing mind may also count towards essence level.</a> If you have 1 lore supernal he could teach your full ciricle his teaching charms by essence 3 at the end of every story you could have all your solars get into a giant circle jerk of teaching having each of them give their earned Solar and Normal Exp to each other as normal XP. At that point they could only &quot;spend&quot; The teaching gained xp saving their normal xp for teaching and then use that to raise themselves to new even higher amounts of xp. <br /> <br /> Also you can uses Power Awarding Prana to teach yourself charms committing the motes and use teaching charms to Teach that new charm to other solars in your group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","user":"WalkingEye","date":". 07-04-2018, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T11:21:07-07:00","id":1232448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232446#post1232446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exp you commit to Flowing Mind Prana is Committed until recovered So it is always a net positive amount of exp.</div> </div> </div> </div>armyofwhisper's point, however, is that the XP you use to activate <i>Tireless Learner Method</i> are <i>not</i> committed. They're just lost. Every time you use it, you're basically gambling that you'll get more successes than the number of dice you're rolling - <i>two</i> more successes, in fact. Even re-rolling failures, that's not a very good bet.<br /> <br /> Anyway, though, could we please take the discussion of Lore charms elsewhere? They're not really on-topic in a Craft thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T11:41:07-07:00","id":1232459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232448#post1232448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> armyofwhisper's point, however, is that the XP you use to activate <i>Tireless Learner Method</i> are <i>not</i> committed. They're just lost. Every time you use it, you're basically gambling that you'll get more successes than the number of dice you're rolling - <i>two</i> more successes, in fact. Even re-rolling failures, that's not a very good bet.<br /> <br /> Anyway, though, could we please take the discussion of Lore charms elsewhere? They're not really on-topic in a Craft thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you use Spirit-Stoking Elevation to pay for it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T12:18:07-07:00","id":1232465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232417#post1232417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in the link I have to the houserules I use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having read over this, I wanted to say thanks! It basically seems to cover all the thoughts I had about condensing the Craft charms, and the new effects are very nice as well. I'm basically planning on implementing it wholesale in my own game (if anyone takes Craft, which no-one has done so far).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T13:51:04-07:00","id":1232477,"title":"","content":"I decided to write up that &quot;encode intimacy&quot; charm I was thinking about. What do people think?<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Passion-Reifing Artistry</span></b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 1gxp; <b>Mins: </b>Craft 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One crafting project<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Object-Strengthening Touch<br /> <br /> A Lawgiver artisan puts something of themselves into everything they craft. With this charm, this becomes vastly more pronounced - the fruits of their labor uphold their passions and motivations even in the hands of others.<br /> <br /> This charm is activated at the beginning of a major or greater project, and the motes remained committed until the project is completed. The Solar must declare one of their intimacies they are embedding within the object - this can be any level for a major project, while a superior project requires major or better intensity, and a legendary project must be defining. Once the project is successfully completed, the nature of the intimacy, both its target and its context, will be obvious to anyone who rolls (Perception + either Craft or Socialize) while scrutinising it. <br /> <br /> Anyone who using the object for its intended purpose in a manner that would uphold or support the encoded intimacy gains 1 non-charm die on any rolls required. This stacks with bonuses for exceptional equipment, if the object is such. If a user shares the intimacy, at the same level as the original creator, they receive additional bonuses: for a major project, or a mundane superior project, if they spend willpower on a roll that support's the object's intimacy, the user adds two successes, rather than just one, to their result. For an artifact superior project, or a legendary project, the item automatically gains an evocation that unlocks for free for any user who shares the intimacy at the same level. The GM and the player should collaborate to determine the details of this evocation - it should be appropriate for Essence 1 characters, and relate to the intimacy in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T14:07:04-07:00","id":1232482,"title":"","content":"Why non-charm dice? I'm generally wary of that, it can get busted. I don't see a reason why it can't be charm dice.<br /> Also, you mention dice at the beginning and then successes later (when saying major intimacies give 2).<br /> <br /> Overall though I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T14:17:02-07:00","id":1232484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232482#post1232482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why non-charm dice? I'm generally wary of that, it can get busted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize that, but a) I think 1 probably isn't going to break things, b) I want this to benefit mortals too, and I'm not even sure they <i>get</i> charm dice, and c) 1 non-charm die is basically the effect of an exceptional item, and I wanted the effect to be more or less in-line with that, at least for lower-level items.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you mention dice at the beginning and then successes later (when saying major intimacies give 2).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's in context of spending willpower on a task, though. It stacks with the earlier bonus. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T14:20:52-07:00","id":1232485,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1533_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1533\" data-vbnamecard=\"1533\">Kelly Pedersen</a> <br /> <br /> \u200bMortals can benefit from &quot;Charm dice&quot;, further, they have no dice cap. The Storyteller is encouraged to set whatever cap they believe is adequate for a mortal to benefit from in each situation.<br /> <br /> At least that is what I recall from Dev discussion on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T15:32:41-07:00","id":1232492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232440#post1232440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, nevermind the question about the link to these - I spotted the link you posted upthread, and that one works. Apologies again for the misunderstanding!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, just did notice the 404 on my signature (I normally turn them off actually) so went back and fixed it just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T11:34:20-07:00","id":1232890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1232465#post1232465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having read over this, I wanted to say thanks! It basically seems to cover all the thoughts I had about condensing the Craft charms, and the new effects are very nice as well. I'm basically planning on implementing it wholesale in my own game (if anyone takes Craft, which no-one has done so far).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope you find them useful. I personally am a fan of the set as a whole. It's mostly the works of Nihnoz, who I don't think posts here as often, editted to suit my writing style preferences and such, plus a few more. There's another set about I think which does a similar take (light touch on base system, overhaul of Charms) that I found interesting too. A big reason I prefer this too is that the Dragon-Blooded Charms wrok just fine in this setup, since by not changing the base system you don't really have to do anything with their Charms, which besides some math fixing work fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T01:37:31-07:00","id":1233156,"title":"","content":"I think something overlooked in the &quot;there's no Melee charm to give you XP!&quot; kerfluffle is Melee, Stealth, etc charms DO give you XP, via the little known action of &quot;playing a session of Exalted&quot;. Craft and Lore tend to be background activities. Active play means fulfilling the requirements for solar XP and dedicated crafters only get to really engage with that side somewhat. At least, I presume that's the operative theory. Given the investment needed and actual play, I concur - they aren't really a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T03:31:56-07:00","id":1233163,"title":"","content":"While I don't really feel like getting into the whole Charms that give you XP/things that cost XP thing, that's not really a good view on it.<br /> <br /> One of the explicit design goals for 3e is the removal of any Ability as a downtime only trait. Craft and Lore both received new systems that heavily emphasize using them in active play.<br /> <br /> Since this is a thread about Craft and all, sticking to that: The Expression Solar XP bonus and the crafting basic objectives actually overlap significantly if a Craft focused character has an Intimacy (or multiples) related to their craft that's Major or Defining. It doesn't have to be some big flashing act of crafting, you can do it with a low-key Basic project if you tie it into your Intimacy strongly enough/entertainingly enough. The Role Solar XP bonus is really simple to get for Twilight craftspeople, and not that rough for everyone else but Dawns; but you can always get the Role bonus by ceding spotlight time.<br /> <br /> So when it comes to what seems to be the original dev's design theories, it seems a bit more operative to assume that they were kind of acknowledging that Craft is an XP sink. This isn't even getting into the size of the Craft Charm trees, but things like Supreme Celestial Focus. The whole point of Supreme Celestial Focus isn't about whether or not you're going to hit the Solar XP bonuses with Craft, but making the need to buy each craft skill set your character has as an additional 0-5 Ability less taxing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T05:01:31-07:00","id":1233169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1233163#post1233163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So when it comes to what seems to be the original dev's design theories, it seems a bit more operative to assume that they were kind of acknowledging that Craft is an XP sink. This isn't even getting into the size of the Craft Charm trees, but things like Supreme Celestial Focus. The whole point of Supreme Celestial Focus isn't about whether or not you're going to hit the Solar XP bonuses with Craft, but making the need to buy each craft skill set your character has as an additional 0-5 Ability less taxing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This made me think of a key point for Kelly;<br /> If you're designing a Craft charmset, making buying all those Craft abilities less onerous is probably something pretty important. DBs don't seem to be able to do that, but they are the weakest Exalts. Solars do it quite easily; most of the Craft dots I've bought are with Craft XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T05:24:59-07:00","id":1233172,"title":"","content":"Robert Vance suggested if not outright declared that you don't necessarily need dots in a mundane Craft for storyteller approved projects in that mundane Craft. That helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T05:39:10-07:00","id":1233175,"title":"","content":"Naturally; one doesn't need dots in Brawl to throw a punch, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T07:01:39-07:00","id":1233183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1233169#post1233169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This made me think of a key point for Kelly;<br /> If you're designing a Craft charmset, making buying all those Craft abilities less onerous is probably something pretty important. DBs don't seem to be able to do that, but they are the weakest Exalts. Solars do it quite easily; most of the Craft dots I've bought are with Craft XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>While any new craft charm set should interact with the system we've got, it's worth mentioning that one of the Houserules in Kelly's game is that craft is treated as lore is. IE you purchase dots once and then buy specialties to increase your areas of expertise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T07:10:42-07:00","id":1233187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robert Vance suggested if not outright declared that you don't necessarily need dots in a mundane Craft for storyteller approved projects in that mundane Craft. That helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly, but just because you can make Craft checks with 0 dots doesn't mean you're good at Crafting. The sort of people who want to buy Craft charms are going to want more than 0 dots in their 2nd and 3rd Craft ability.<br /> I myself have 22 dots in Craft. My original 5 only covered Weaponsmithing (and similar things at +1 difficulty) which made doing things like building houses and boats quite difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-08-2018, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T07:34:14-07:00","id":1233194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1233183#post1233183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While any new craft charm set should interact with the system we've got, it's worth mentioning that one of the Houserules in Kelly's game is that craft is treated as lore is. IE you purchase dots once and then buy specialties to increase your areas of expertise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, in that case it's not so important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T07:40:53-07:00","id":1233195,"title":"","content":"So I was thinking a bit more about Supreme Perfection of Craft. As a number of people said earlier, it's rather overpowered.<br /> However, it's timing rules are good.<br /> <br /> The current Craft rules were created to solve a specific problem.<br /> <br /> In the old rules, Craft was a matter of time. And this meant that creating artefacts was incredibly awkward in games without a lot of downtime. On the other hand, if you did have a lot of downtime, you could churn out daiklaives like a production line, which Morke and Holden were not big fans of.<br /> <br /> So, they created a system where you get points while adventuring, and then spend those points to make artefacts. You need some time, but not that much (with charms, just a few weeks for level 2-4).<br /> So, if you have only a bit of downtime because you're always rushing around adventuring, you should hopefully generate enough points to make some artefacts, but if you do have a ton of downtime, you can't churn out loads of artefacts because you'll run out of points.<br /> <br /> And Supreme Perfection works with this, because it gives you points either per day, or per downtime. I managed to make 2 artefacts after 1 story, but that used nearly all my Crafting XP. I then had a month of downtime, but didn't really get a lot of points back. And if I had another year of downtime, I'd have plenty of time to make artefacts... but no Craft points to make them with.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, if you do make a point-generating charm, while it should perhaps be less powerful than Supreme Perfection (and have less speed-bump prereqs), having it give out rewards at the same rate as Supreme Perfection I think is fine.<br /> (There are several other charms that give out craft XP per story; I think that's too slow. Maybe if they gave out loads, but they only give a little. I think better to have a charm that gives you a little every day/downtime.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T13:01:46-07:00","id":1233251,"title":"","content":"On the XP thing:<br /> <br /> While it it is less relevant in you turn new crafts into specialties instead of full 0-5 traits, it is important to remember that there's still XP costs to that; esp. with Artifacts and Manses both requiring a unique craft that a lot of characters aren't going to start with. This can be pretty harsh in the RAW because you use the lower of your normal craft and Craft (Artifact), and artifice is hard if you're using Craft (Artifact) 1 for your dice-pool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1232172-discussing-issues-with-the-solar-craft-charm-set?p=1233195#post1233195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it's timing rules are good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if this is the case as much as the &quot;story&quot; time unit is treated as bigger than it is.<br /> <br /> I generally have an impression (though this goes back to before Exalted, since it's a ST system thing that's been around for a long time) that people frequently will go dozens of sessions before considering a single story over, while the books usually are written that a story should only be a few sessions. Like, in my games, a story is usually 3-5 sessions (not purposefully so, but generally each session encompasses an &quot;act&quot; in a traditional theatrical sense, esp. since the five-act structure is something that overlaps well with European and Asian source material).<br /> <br /> Prolonged downtimes are almost always a marker that one story has ended, and another has begun for me. If people in my normal group hear &quot;a month of downtime,&quot; they also hear, &quot;story over, anything that triggers such as Charm resets, cxp rewards, etc all happen now,&quot; unless it's been clear that the current course of the game is operating on long periods of time in general.<br /> <br /> So &quot;at the end of a story&quot; works fine for us, because that's a fairly frequent event for the players.<br /> <br /> I think Supreme Perfection of Craft's timing system has an issue because it doesn't... interact with anything to justify it's frequency rates. Like, mote recovery operates on a similar concept, but it interacts with the &quot;action pacing&quot; of what's going on. Players get into the adrenaline rush like burst of motes during high action scenes even if it doesn't have a distinct in-game reasoning (which is fine). As long as the day is busy enough to not be downtime, you get cxp because... magic? Crafting doesn't have to be part of it, some sort of insight doesn't have to be part of it. Just.... doing something.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure the Supreme Perfection of Craft timing would look more appealing if the game did more to say how frequently stories are expected to happen for what the developers envisioned for those effects, and then did something like say, &quot;if your game's stories happen less frequently, find a good low point in the action to give out those mechanics in the middle of stories.&quot; Since to me, it seems like that's better for the overall flow of things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}